Crisp-seared chicken baked in a tropical sweet Hawaiian sauce with vibrant red bell pepper and pineapple tidbits.

*Adapted from [The Recipe Critic](https://therecipecritic.com/2015/07/baked-sweet-hawaiian-chicken/).*

## Ingredients

### Chicken
- 3–4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts, cut into bite-sized pieces
- Salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 1 ½ cups cornstarch
- 3 large eggs, beaten
- ¼ cup canola oil (for searing)

### Sweet Hawaiian Sauce
- 1 cup pineapple juice
- ½ cup brown sugar
- ⅓ cup soy sauce
- 1 teaspoon minced garlic
- ½ tablespoon cornstarch
- 1 red bell pepper, chopped
- 1 can (20 oz) pineapple tidbits, drained

## Instructions

1. **Prep Chicken and Dredging Bowls:** Heat oven to 325°F (165°C) and coat a 9x13-inch baking pan with nonstick spray. Cut the boneless chicken breasts into bite-sized chunks; season with salt and black pepper. Fill one shallow dish with cornstarch and a second with the whisked eggs.
2. **Cornstarch-and-Egg Coating:** Dip each piece of chicken into the cornstarch, turning to coat all sides and shaking free loose starch, then plunge into the beaten egg to seal.
3. **Brown in the Skillet:** Warm ¼ cup canola oil in a wide frying pan over medium-high heat. Working in batches to avoid crowding, fry the chicken chunks for roughly 2 minutes until the crust turns golden on all sides (the meat will cook through in the oven). Shift seared chicken into the prepared baking dish.
4. **Mix Pineapple Glaze:** In a mixing bowl, blend the pineapple juice, brown sugar, soy sauce, minced garlic, and ½ tablespoon cornstarch until sugar dissolves. Fold in the chopped red bell pepper and drained pineapple chunks.
5. **Slow Bake with Glaze:** Pour the sweet pineapple mixture over the chicken. Bake uncovered at 325°F for 1 hour. Give the pan a thorough stir every 15 minutes, which pulls the caramelized syrup up and over the crispy chicken crust.
6. **Rest and Dish Up:** Allow the pan to rest for 5 minutes after removing from the oven so the glaze thickens. Spoon generously over fluffy steamed jasmine or long-grain white rice.

## Notes

- **Stirring is Key:** Stirring every 15 minutes allows the cornstarch-egg crust on the chicken to soak up the sauce and form a sticky glaze without burning.
- **Bell Pepper Variations:** Add green or yellow bell peppers for additional color and crunch.
